#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:28
msgid ""
"Guido van Rossum named the language after *Monty Python's Flying Circus*, "
"not the snake."
msgstr ""
"Guido van Rossum puso al lenguaje el nombre por *Monty Python's Flying "
"Circus*, no por la serpiente."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:32
msgid "Who created the Python programming language?"
msgstr "¿Quién creó el lenguaje de programación Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:41
msgid "Linus Torvalds."
msgstr "Linus Torvalds."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:42
msgid "Dennis Ritchie."
msgstr "Dennis Ritchie."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:43
msgid "Guido van Rossum."
msgstr "Guido van Rossum."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:44
msgid "James Gosling."
msgstr "James Gosling."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:49
msgid ""
"Guido van Rossum started Python in late 1989 and released the first version "
"in 1991."
msgstr ""
"Guido van Rossum empezó Python a finales de 1989 y publicó la primera "
"versión en 1991."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:53
msgid "In what year was Python first released?"
msgstr "¿En qué año se publicó Python por primera vez?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:70
msgid "Guido van Rossum published the first release of Python in 1991."
msgstr "Guido van Rossum publicó la primera versión de Python en 1991."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:73
msgid "What is the standard file extension for Python source files?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cuál es la extensión de archivo estándar para los archivos fuente de "
"Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:82
msgid "``.pt``"
msgstr "``.pt``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:83
msgid "``.pyt``"
msgstr "``.pyt``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:84
msgid "``.py``"
msgstr "``.py``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:85
msgid "``.python``"
msgstr "``.python``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:90
msgid "Python source files use the ``.py`` extension."
msgstr "Los archivos fuente de Python usan la extensión ``.py``."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:93
msgid "Which major version of Python is actively supported today?"
msgstr "¿Qué versión principal de Python tiene soporte activo hoy en día?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:102
msgid "Python 1."
msgstr "Python 1."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:103
msgid "Python 2."
msgstr "Python 2."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:104
msgid "Python 3."
msgstr "Python 3."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:105
msgid "Python 5."
msgstr "Python 5."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:110
msgid ""
"Python 3 is the current, supported line. Python 2 reached end of life on "
"January 1, 2020."
msgstr ""
"Python 3 es la línea actual y con soporte. Python 2 llegó al final de su "
"vida útil el 1 de enero de 2020."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:114
msgid "What is the name of Python's official third-party package repository?"
msgstr ""
"¿Cómo se llama el repositorio oficial de paquetes de terceros de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:123
msgid "npm."
msgstr "npm."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:124
msgid "PyPI."
msgstr "PyPI."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:125
msgid "PythonHouse."
msgstr "PythonHouse."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:126
msgid "CRAN."
msgstr "CRAN."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:131
msgid ""
"PyPI, the Python Package Index, hosts the third-party packages you install "
"with ``pip``. npm belongs to Node.js and CRAN to R; \"PythonHouse\" is not a"
" real thing."
msgstr ""
"PyPI, el Python Package Index, aloja los paquetes de terceros que instalas "
"con ``pip``. npm pertenece a Node.js y CRAN a R; \"PythonHouse\" no existe."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:136
msgid ""
"What command do you normally use to install a third-party Python package?"
msgstr ""
"¿Qué comando sueles usar para instalar un paquete de terceros en Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:145
msgid "``python get``"
msgstr "``python get``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:146
msgid "``apt install``"
msgstr "``apt install``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:147
msgid "``pip install``"
msgstr "``pip install``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:148
msgid "``import``"
msgstr "``import``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:153
msgid ""
"``pip install <package>`` downloads a package from PyPI and installs it into"
" your environment."
msgstr ""
"``pip install <paquete>`` descarga un paquete de PyPI y lo instala en tu "
"entorno."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:157
msgid "What is the official website for the Python language?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es el sitio web oficial del lenguaje Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:166
msgid "``python.com``"
msgstr "``python.com``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:167
msgid "``getpython.io``"
msgstr "``getpython.io``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:168
msgid "``python.org``"
msgstr "``python.org``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:169
msgid "``python.dev``"
msgstr "``python.dev``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:174
msgid ""
"``python.org`` is the official home of Python: downloads, documentation, and"
" the news that surrounds the language."
msgstr ""
"``python.org`` es la web oficial de Python: descargas, documentación y las "
"novedades del lenguaje."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:178
msgid "Which organization stewards the Python language today?"
msgstr "¿Qué organización gestiona hoy el lenguaje Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:187
msgid "The Linux Foundation."
msgstr "La Linux Foundation."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:188
msgid "The Python Software Foundation (PSF)."
msgstr "La Python Software Foundation (PSF)."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:189
msgid "Oracle."
msgstr "Oracle."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:190
msgid "The Free Software Foundation."
msgstr "La Free Software Foundation."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:195
msgid ""
"The Python Software Foundation (PSF) is the non-profit that holds the "
"intellectual property and supports the Python community."
msgstr ""
"La Python Software Foundation (PSF) es la organización sin ánimo de lucro "
"que posee la propiedad intelectual y da soporte a la comunidad de Python."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:199
msgid "Which of these is a popular Python web framework?"
msgstr "¿Cuál de estos es un framework web popular de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:208
msgid "Laravel."
msgstr "Laravel."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:209
msgid "Rails."
msgstr "Rails."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:210
msgid "Django."
msgstr "Django."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:211
msgid "Spring."
msgstr "Spring."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:216
msgid ""
"Django is one of the best-known Python web frameworks. Laravel is PHP, Rails"
" is Ruby, and Spring is Java."
msgstr ""
"Django es uno de los frameworks web de Python más conocidos. Laravel es de "
"PHP, Rails de Ruby y Spring de Java."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:220
msgid "What is the default prompt of Python's interactive interpreter?"
msgstr "¿Cuál es el prompt por defecto del intérprete interactivo de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:229
msgid "``$``"
msgstr "``$``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:230
msgid "``>>>``"
msgstr "``>>>``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:231
msgid "``#``"
msgstr "``#``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:232
msgid "``py>``"
msgstr "``py>``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:237
msgid "The Python REPL prompts you with ``>>>`` for each new statement."
msgstr "El REPL de Python te muestra ``>>>`` para cada nueva instrucción."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:240
msgid "What does Python's logo depict?"
msgstr "¿Qué representa el logotipo de Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:249
msgid "A single coiled snake."
msgstr "Una única serpiente enroscada."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:250
msgid "Two intertwined snakes."
msgstr "Dos serpientes entrelazadas."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:251
msgid "A circus tent."
msgstr "Una carpa de circo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:252
msgid "A blue elephant."
msgstr "Un elefante azul."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:257
msgid ""
"The modern Python logo shows two stylized, intertwined snakes in blue and "
"yellow."
msgstr ""
"El logotipo moderno de Python muestra dos serpientes estilizadas y "
"entrelazadas en azul y amarillo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:261
msgid "How does Python group blocks of code?"
msgstr "¿Cómo agrupa Python los bloques de código?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:270
msgid "With ``begin`` and ``end`` keywords."
msgstr "Con las palabras clave ``begin`` y ``end``."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:271
#, python-brace-format
msgid "With curly braces ``{ }``."
msgstr "Con llaves ``{ }``."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:272
msgid "With indentation."
msgstr "Con la indentación."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:273
msgid "With parentheses ``( )``."
msgstr "Con paréntesis ``( )``."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:278
msgid ""
"Python uses indentation (leading whitespace) to define blocks, instead of "
"braces or keywords."
msgstr ""
"Python usa la indentación (el espacio en blanco inicial) para definir "
"bloques, en lugar de llaves o palabras clave."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:282
msgid "Is Python case-sensitive?"
msgstr "¿Python distingue entre mayúsculas y minúsculas?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:291
msgid "No, ``Name`` and ``name`` are the same."
msgstr "No, ``Name`` y ``name`` son lo mismo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:292
msgid "Yes, ``Name`` and ``name`` are different."
msgstr "Sí, ``Name`` y ``name`` son distintos."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:293
msgid "Only inside functions."
msgstr "Solo dentro de las funciones."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:294
msgid "Only for built-in names."
msgstr "Solo para los nombres incorporados."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:299
msgid ""
"Python is case-sensitive: ``Name``, ``name``, and ``NAME`` are three "
"different identifiers."
msgstr ""
"Python distingue mayúsculas y minúsculas: ``Name``, ``name`` y ``NAME`` son "
"tres identificadores distintos."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:303
msgid "Python is best described as which kind of language?"
msgstr "¿Cómo se describe mejor Python como lenguaje?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:312
msgid "A markup language."
msgstr "Un lenguaje de marcado."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:313
msgid ""
"A language that must be compiled to a standalone ``.exe`` before running."
msgstr ""
"Un lenguaje que debe compilarse a un ``.exe`` independiente antes de "
"ejecutarse."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:314
msgid "An interpreted, high-level language."
msgstr "Un lenguaje interpretado y de alto nivel."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:315
msgid "A hardware description language."
msgstr "Un lenguaje de descripción de hardware."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:320
msgid ""
"Python is a high-level, interpreted language: you run source files directly "
"without a separate compile step."
msgstr ""
"Python es un lenguaje interpretado y de alto nivel: ejecutas los archivos "
"fuente directamente, sin un paso de compilación aparte."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:324
msgid "How is typing handled in Python?"
msgstr "¿Cómo se gestiona el tipado en Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:333
msgid "You must declare every variable's type."
msgstr "Hay que declarar el tipo de cada variable."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:334
msgid "Variables are dynamically typed."
msgstr "Las variables tienen tipado dinámico."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:335
msgid "Every variable is a string until converted."
msgstr "Toda variable es una cadena hasta que se convierte."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:336
msgid "Types cannot change once assigned."
msgstr "Los tipos no pueden cambiar una vez asignados."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:341
msgid ""
"Python is dynamically typed: a variable takes the type of whatever value you"
" assign to it, and that can change over time."
msgstr ""
"Python tiene tipado dinámico: una variable toma el tipo del valor que le "
"asignes, y ese tipo puede cambiar con el tiempo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:345
msgid "What does the ``print()`` function do?"
msgstr "¿Qué hace la función ``print()``?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:354
msgid "Sends the text to the printer."
msgstr "Envía el texto a la impresora."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:355
msgid "Writes its arguments to standard output."
msgstr "Escribe sus argumentos en la salida estándar."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:356
msgid "Saves the text to a file."
msgstr "Guarda el texto en un fichero."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:357
msgid "Returns the text without showing it."
msgstr "Devuelve el texto sin mostrarlo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:362
msgid ""
"``print()`` writes its arguments to standard output (normally the screen), "
"separated by spaces and followed by a newline."
msgstr ""
"``print()`` escribe sus argumentos en la salida estándar (normalmente la "
"pantalla), separados por espacios y seguidos de un salto de línea."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:366
msgid "What is the name of the largest annual community Python conference?"
msgstr "¿Cómo se llama la mayor conferencia anual de la comunidad Python?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:375
msgid "PyDay."
msgstr "PyDay."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:376
msgid "SnakeConf."
msgstr "SnakeConf."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:377
msgid "PyCon."
msgstr "PyCon."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:378
msgid "DjangoCon."
msgstr "DjangoCon."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:383
msgid ""
"PyCon is the flagship community conference for Python, held in many "
"countries around the world."
msgstr ""
"PyCon es la conferencia comunitaria de referencia de Python, celebrada en "
"muchos países del mundo."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:387
msgid "What does this program print?"
msgstr "¿Qué imprime este programa?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:400
msgid "``Hello world``"
msgstr "``Hello world``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:401
msgid "``Hello, world!``"
msgstr "``Hello, world!``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:402
msgid "``\"Hello, world!\"``"
msgstr "``\"Hello, world!\"``"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:403
msgid "Nothing."
msgstr "Nada."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:408
msgid ""
"``print`` writes its argument to the screen exactly, including the comma and"
" exclamation mark."
msgstr ""
"``print`` escribe su argumento en la pantalla tal cual, incluyendo la coma y"
" el signo de exclamación."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:412
msgid "Which statement about Python's licensing is true?"
msgstr "¿Cuál de estas afirmaciones sobre la licencia de Python es cierta?"

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:421
msgid "It is proprietary and closed source."
msgstr "Es propietario y de código cerrado."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:422
msgid "It requires a paid license for commercial use."
msgstr "Requiere una licencia de pago para uso comercial."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:423
msgid "It is free and open source."
msgstr "Es libre y de código abierto."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:424
msgid "It can only be used for education."
msgstr "Solo puede usarse con fines educativos."

#: ../../../culture-easy.rst:429
msgid ""
"Python is free and open source, developed openly by the Python Software "
"Foundation and a global community."
msgstr ""
"Python es libre y de código abierto, desarrollado de forma abierta por la "
"Python Software Foundation y una comunidad global."

